{"format":1,"key":"zone:gnomeregan","path":"/lore/zone/gnomeregan","name":"Gnomeregan","kind":"dungeon","label":"Dungeon","zone":{"key":"gnomeregan","name":"Gnomeregan","path":"/lore/zone/gnomeregan"},"levels":"Levels 29-38","description":"Carved into the snowy foothills of Dun Morogh, Gnomeregan was once the subterranean capital and greatest technological wonder of the gnomish race. Today…","intro":[],"clips":[{"id":"zone:gnomeregan","part":"narration","anchor":"story","title":"The story","paras":["Carved into the snowy foothills of Dun Morogh, Gnomeregan was once the subterranean capital and greatest technological wonder of the gnomish race. Today it lies ruined and quarantined, poisoned by radioactive fallout following a desperate defense against an underground trogg invasion. Its surviving people now dwell as refugees in nearby Ironforge, while the irradiated halls remain overrun by mutated troggs, deranged leper gnomes, and rogue mechanical sentries.","Long before its tragic fall, Gnomeregan stood as a testament to the heights of gnomish brilliance, ambition, and industry. Constructed with the assistance of the nearby dwarves of Ironforge, the sprawling mechanical complex was powered by giant grinding engines, whirring gears, and an intricate ventilation network that required fifteen technicians working around the clock just to maintain fresh air. It was a thriving center of invention, competitive craft, and politics centered on Tinkers' Court, serving as the proud capital from which gnomes contributed invaluable siege engines, flying machines, and armaments to the Alliance of Lordaeron during the Second War.","Around the time the Scourge tore through Lordaeron during the Third War, a subterranean nightmare stirred beneath Dun Morogh. Unwitting dwarven excavations at the ancient titan vault of Uldaman awakened hordes of primitive troggs, which burrowed into the lower foundations of Gnomeregan. High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque and his forces fought a desperate war against the invaders. When defenses collapsed, Mekkatorque yielded to the counsel of his chief advisor, Mekgineer Thermaplugg, and authorized venting the city's radioactive waste tanks into the lower levels to eradicate the troggs. Instead, the toxic gas spread uncontrollable catastrophe, wiping out nearly eighty percent of the gnomish population in days."],"hash":"4660a3","voices":{"male-narrator":{"sha":"148d789d1d","sec":108},"female-narrator":{"sha":"367b4a3a7b","sec":120}}}],"sources":[{"kind":"wiki","title":"Gnomeregan","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Gnomeregan"}],"related":[{"p":"/lore/npc/gelbin-mekkatorque","n":"Gelbin Mekkatorque","k":"npc"},{"p":"/lore/npc/sicco-thermaplugg","n":"Mekgineer Thermaplugg","k":"boss"},{"p":"/lore/zone/dunmorogh","n":"Dun Morogh","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/zone/ironforge","n":"Ironforge","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/topic/gnome","n":"Gnome","k":"topic"},{"p":"/lore/topic/trogg","n":"Trogg","k":"topic"},{"p":"/lore/topic/leper-gnome","n":"Leper gnome","k":"topic"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/tinkers-court","n":"Tinkers' Court","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/brewnall-village","n":"Brewnall Village","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/chill-breeze-valley","n":"Chill Breeze Valley","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/frostmane-hold","n":"Frostmane Hold","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/ironforge","n":"Ironforge","k":"subzone"}],"children":[{"p":"/lore/subzone/clean-zone","n":"Clean Zone","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/clockwerk-run","n":"Clockwerk Run","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/dormitory","n":"Dormitory","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/engineering-labs","n":"Engineering Labs","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/hall-of-gears","n":"Hall of Gears","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/launch-bay","n":"Launch Bay","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/loading-room","n":"Loading Room","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/tinkers-court","n":"Tinkers' Court","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/train-depot","n":"Train Depot","k":"subzon